hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"63","Allahumma inni as'aluka ya Allah bi'annaka al-Wahid al-Ahad al-Samad alladhi lam yalid wa lam yulad, wa lam yakun lahu kufuwan ahad, an taghfir li dhunubika innaka anta al-Ghafur al-Rahim.. O Allah, I ask You, O Allah, by Your being the One, the Only, the Eternal, the Absolute, who neither begets nor is begotten, and there is none like unto Him, to forgive my sins. Indeed, You are the Most Forgiving, the Most Merciful."
"64","Allahumma inni as'aluka bi-anna laka al-hamdu la ilaha illa Anta, wahdaka la sharika laka, al-Mannan, ya Badi' al-samawati wa al-ardhi, ya Dhal-Jalali wal-Ikram, ya Hayyu ya Qayyum, inni as'aluka al-jannata wa a'udhu bika min al-nar.. O Allah, I ask You, for all praise is due to You; there is no god but You alone, without partner, the Bestower, Originator of the heavens and the earth, O Possessor of majesty and honor, O Ever-Living, O Self-Subsisting, I ask You for Paradise and seek Your protection from the Fire."
